# Form Builder – Project Status

## Stack
- **Frontend:** React 18 + Vite 8 + TypeScript
- **Backend:** None (client will call PayloadCMS API directly)
- **Target:** PayloadCMS Form Builder plugin / forms collection

## Credentials (where to set them)
- **Environment file:** Copy `frontend/.env.example` to `frontend/.env`. Set:
  - `VITE_PAYLOAD_API_URL` – Payload API base URL (e.g. `http://localhost:3000` in dev; HTTPS public URL in production builds)
  - `VITE_PAYLOAD_AUTH_SLUG` – Auth collection slug (usually `users`)
  - Optionally `VITE_PAYLOAD_ADMIN_EMAIL` and `VITE_PAYLOAD_ADMIN_PASSWORD` – **dev only** (Vite dev server): auto-login and login form pre-fill. Omit for production builds; auth is always via the login page.
- **VPS / Cloudflare:** `deploy/ecosystem.config.cjs` (PM2) and `deploy/nginx-forms.yallaprojects.com.conf` (reverse proxy to the app on port 4173).
- **In-app login:** Email and password can be entered in a login form; they are sent to Payload’s login endpoint and never stored. The returned JWT is stored in `sessionStorage` (see `src/api/auth.ts`).
- `.env` is gitignored; do not commit credentials.

## Current phase
Form builder with live preview and pagination. List forms; create/edit with field palette and props panel; live app-style preview (modal layout, required asterisks, all field types); page-break block for preview pagination (Previous/Next); help text/description and message-as-section heading; fully customizable fields like Payload. Save filters out pageBreak so Payload only receives standard blocks.

## Directory structure
```
src/
  api/        – Payload API client, auth, requests
  components/– Reusable UI (form fields, builder blocks, etc.)
  hooks/     – React hooks (auth, form state, etc.)
  layouts/   – Page layouts
  lib/       – Shared utilities
  pages/     – Route-level views
  store/     – Global state (if needed)
  types/     – TypeScript types (Payload form schema, etc.)
```

